  "note": "Election of the Kilkeel Urban Council, poll due Wednesday 18 May 1955. Ten candidates were nominated for nine seats, but Mr. Patrick Joseph M'Conville withdrew, leaving nine for nine; all were returned unopposed (Belfast News-Letter, 5 and 6 May 1955, pp. 6 and 10). The withdrawal report states: 'For the Kilkeel Urban Council there will be no election, Mr. Patrick Joseph M'Conville having withdrawn.' Returned unopposed."
